  "final_text": "**On paper, Wartapak (Poznań) is cheapest. But it's the only offer that matches what you asked for, a price delivered to your plant, that's actually all-in, and that one is Rednitz (Nürnberg).** Wartapak and Kartovka quote ex works, so you'd still have to pay for shipping, and neither says what that would cost.\n\n### Cost for 40,000 boxes per year (net, before VAT)\n\n| | A Rednitz, Nürnberg | B Wartapak, Poznań | C Kartovka, Brno |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Unit price | €0.66 | €0.52 (€520 per 1,000) | €0.575 (€57.50 per 100) |\n| One-time tooling | none | €1,450 | none |\n| **Total at quoted price** | **€26,400** | **€22,250** | **€23,000** |\n| Early-payment discount | 2% in 14 days | 2% in 10 days (not on tooling) | 3% in 10 days |\n| **Total with discount** | **€25,872** (€0.647/box) | **€21,834** (€0.546/box) | **€22,310** (€0.558/box) |\n| Delivery term | DAP: delivered to your plant | EXW Poznań: you collect and load | FCA Brno: you collect, they load |\n| Freight to Nordhessen | included | **not included**, 2 trips of 20,000 | **not included**, 4 trips of 10,000 |\n\n### How much shipping B and C can cost before A wins\n- **B vs. A:** B is about €4,040 cheaper, which covers roughly **€2,000 per trip** across 2 trips. Each trip is 20,000 boxes, about 20 pallets (going by Kartovka's 10,000 boxes = 10 pallets).\n- **C vs. A:** C is about €3,560 cheaper, which covers only about **€890 per trip** across 4 trips of 10 pallets each. That's tight for about 600 km.\n- **B vs. C:** B is €476 cheaper and needs half as many trips, so B beats C in almost any case.\n\n### Other things that affect the decision\n- **Kartovka adds a paper surcharge with no cap.** If their paper index rises 10%, you pay about €1,380 more, and that amount gets no discount. Their offer also expires 30 days after 16 Oct, around 15 Nov 2026.\n- **Price validity:** Rednitz fixes its price for orders through the end of 2027. Wartapak's offer is valid until 30 Nov 2026, and it doesn't say whether the price holds for all of 2027.\n- **Order size and storage:** Rednitz delivers 3,000+ boxes per order in 5 working days, which fits ordering as you need them. Wartapak needs 20,000 per order, half your yearly volume, so you'd store about 20 pallets at a time. Kartovka ships 10,000 per lot.\n\n**My recommendation:** Get a freight quote for 2 full trucks from Poznań to Nordhessen. If it comes in well under about €2,000 per truck, Wartapak is cheapest. Before you commit, ask them to confirm the price holds for 2027 and decide whether you can store 20 pallets. If the freight is higher, or you want a fixed price and small orders, go with Rednitz. I wouldn't pick Kartovka: it would only win if freight were very cheap, and the paper surcharge could wipe out its savings.",
